# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights in the flugo-colaboradores React + Vite application.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version resolved by npm)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

### 2. Code Changes
**Modified: src/App.tsx**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the JSX return statement
- Component placement ensures Speed Insights tracks all pages in the application (both dashboard and cadastro pages)

## Implementation Details

### Framework-Specific Approach
Following the Vercel Speed Insights guide for React applications, I used the `@vercel/speed-insights/react` package which provides a React component wrapper around the tracking script for seamless integration.

### Component Placement
The `<SpeedInsights />` component was added to the root App component (`src/App.tsx`) to ensure it's present on all pages. Since this is a single-page application with conditional rendering of different views, placing it at the App level ensures consistent tracking across navigation.

## Verification

### Build Status
✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- Command: `npm run build`
- Result: All TypeScript compilation and Vite bundling completed without issues

### Linter Status
✅ Linter passed with no errors or warnings
- Command: `npm run lint`
- Result: No ESLint violations detected

### Files Modified
1. `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
2. `package-lock.json` - Updated with resolved dependency tree
3. `src/App.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component and import

## Next Steps
After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard (Project → Speed Insights → Enable)
2. Verify the `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` script is loaded on the deployed site
3. Wait for user visits to start seeing performance metrics in the Speed Insights dashboard

## Notes
- The implementation follows React best practices for Vite applications
- No existing functionality was modified or broken
- The Speed Insights component is non-intrusive and won't affect application performance
- Data collection will only begin after the app is deployed to Vercel and Speed Insights is enabled in the dashboard
